{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1310 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "a977dec847ae32f78fc1e4a86d54ec73ef4d7b95980fe2f0a24cb0bd58d86135" :edb/db-before-t 1309 :edb/db-after-t 1310 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534622 50 #inst "2026-10-08T02:42:05.436Z" 13194139534622 true] [17592186198077 1100 "List the elements of the set $A = \\{n \\in \\mathbb{N}: 5n - 2 \\leq 21 \\}$." 13194139534622 false] [17592186198077 1100 "List the elements of the set $A = \\{n \\in \\mathbb{N}: 5n - 2 \\leq 21 \\}.$" 13194139534622 true] [17592186198077 1145 "The elements of the given set are the natural numbers that satisfy the inequality\n\n$$\n5n - 2 \\leq 21\n$$\n\nSo, we first need to solve our inequality for $n{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}5n - 2 & \\le 21 \\\\ 5n & \\le 23 \\\\ n & \\le \\frac{23}{5}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe positive integer solutions of the inequality above are $1,2,3,4$. Therefore, the given set can be written as\n\n$$\nA = \\{1,2,3,4\\}\n$$" 13194139534622 false] [17592186198077 1145 "The elements of the given set are the natural numbers that satisfy the inequality $5n - 2 \\leq 21.$ \n\nSo, we first need to solve our inequality for $n{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5n-2 & \\le 21 \\\\ 5n & \\le 23 \\\\ n & \\le \\frac{23}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe positive integer solutions of the inequality above are $1,2,3,4.$ Therefore, the given set can be written as \n\n$$\nA = \\{1,2,3,4\\}.\n$$" 13194139534622 true] [17592186198087 1100 "List the elements of the set $A = \\{x \\in \\mathbb{Z}: x^2 - 9 \\lt 0\\}$." 13194139534622 false] [17592186198087 1100 "List the elements of the set $A = \\{x \\in \\mathbb{Z}: x^2 - 9 \\lt 0\\}.$" 13194139534622 true] [17592186198087 1145 "The elements of the given set are the integers that satisfy the inequality $x^2 - 9 < 0$.\n\nSo, we first need to solve our inequality for $x{:}$\n$x^{2} - 9\\begin{vmatrix}< 0 \\\\ x^{2}\\end{vmatrix}< 9; \\sqrt{x^{2}} \\mid < \\sqrt{9}; \\mid x \\mid \\mid < 3; - 3 < x \\mid < 3$\n\nThe integer solutions of the inequality above are $0,\\pm1,\\pm2$. Therefore, the given set can be written as\n\n$$\nA = \\{0, \\pm 1, \\pm 2\\}\n$$" 13194139534622 false] [17592186198087 1145 "The elements of the given set are the integers that satisfy the inequality $x^2 - 9 < 0.$\n\nSo, we first need to solve our inequality for $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-9 & <0 \\\\ {x}^{2} & <9 \\\\ \\sqrt{{x}^{2}} & <\\sqrt{9} \\\\ |x| & <3 \\\\ -3<x & <3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe integer solutions of the inequality above are $0,\\pm1,\\pm2.$ Therefore, the given set can be written as \n\n$$\nA = \\{ 0, \\pm 1, \\pm 2\\}.\n$$" 13194139534622 true] [17592186198088 1100 "List the elements of the set $A=\\{k \\in \\mathbb{Z}: \\mid k-1 \\mid \\leq 4 \\}$." 13194139534622 false] [17592186198088 1100 "List the elements of the set $A=\\{k \\in \\mathbb{Z}: |k-1| \\leq 4 \\}.$" 13194139534622 true] [17592186198088 1145 "The elements of the given set are the integers that satisfy the inequality\n\n$$\n\\mid k-1 \\mid \\leq 4\n$$\n\nSo, we first need to solve for $k{:}$\n\n$$\n\\mid k - 1 \\mid \\le 4; - 4 \\le k - 1 \\le 4; - 3 \\le k \\le 5\n$$\n\nThe integer solutions of the above inequality are $-3,-2,-1,0,1,2,3,4,5$.\n\nTherefore, the given set can be written as\n\n$$\nA = \\{0,\\pm1,\\pm2,\\pm3,4,5 \\}\n$$" 13194139534622 false] [17592186198088 1145 "The elements of the given set are the integers that satisfy the inequality $|k-1| \\leq 4.$ So, we first need to solve for $k{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|k-1|\\le 4 \\\\ -4\\le k-1\\le 4 \\\\ -3\\le k\\le 5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe integer solutions of the above inequality are $-3,-2,-1,0,1,2,3,4,5.$ \n\nTherefore, the given set can be written as \n\n$$\nA = \\{0,\\pm1,\\pm2,\\pm3,4,5 \\}.\n$$" 13194139534622 true] [17592186198089 1100 "List the elements of the set $A = \\left\\{ x\\in \\mathbb R \\: :\\:  \\tan \\left(\\dfrac{\\pi x}{2}\\right) = 0  \\right\\}.$" 13194139534622 true] [17592186198089 1100 "List the elements of the set $A = \\left\\{x\\in \\mathbb R \\::\\: \\tan \\left(\\dfrac{\\pi x}{2}\\right) = 0 \\right\\}$." 13194139534622 false] [17592186198089 1145 "Notice that the solutions to the equation\n\n$$\n\\tan \\left(\\dfrac{\\pi x}{2}\\right) = 0\n$$\n\n are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\pi x}{2} & =n\\pi  \\\\ x & =2n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $n\\in\\mathbb Z.$ \n\nSubstituting different values of $n,$ we see that the solutions are\n\n$$\nx = 0,\\, \\pm 2 ,\\, \\pm 4,\\, \\pm 6,\\, \\ldots\n$$\n\nTherefore, our set $A$ is equivalent to \n\n$$\nA= \\{0,\\, \\pm 2 ,\\, \\pm 4,\\, \\pm 6,\\, \\ldots\\}.\n$$" 13194139534622 true] [17592186198089 1145 "Notice that the solutions to the equation\n\n$$\n\\tan \\left(\\dfrac{\\pi x}{2}\\right) = 0\n$$\n\nare given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{πx}{2} &= nπ \\\\\nx &= 2n\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $n\\in\\mathbb Z$.\n\nSubstituting different values of $n$, we see that the solutions are\n\n$$\nx = 0,\\, \\pm 2,\\, \\pm 4,\\, \\pm 6,\\, \\ldots\n$$\n\nTherefore, our set $A$ is equivalent to\n\n$$\nA= \\{0,\\, \\pm 2,\\, \\pm 4,\\, \\pm 6,\\, \\ldots\\}\n$$" 13194139534622 false] [17592186198192 1020 #edb/ref 17592186299341 13194139534622 true] [17592186198192 1020 #edb/ref 17592186299348 13194139534622 true] [17592186198192 1020 #edb/ref 17592186299355 13194139534622 true] [17592186198192 1020 #edb/ref 17592186299369 13194139534622 true] [17592186198192 1020 #edb/ref 17592186299376 13194139534622 true] [17592186198193 1020 #edb/ref 17592186299362 13194139534622 true] [17592186198193 1020 #edb/ref 17592186299425 13194139534622 true] [17592186198193 1020 #edb/ref 17592186299432 13194139534622 true] [17592186198193 1020 #edb/ref 17592186299446 13194139534622 true] [17592186198193 1020 #edb/ref 17592186299453 13194139534622 true] [17592186198194 1020 #edb/ref 17592186299383 13194139534622 true] [17592186198194 1020 #edb/ref 17592186299390 13194139534622 true] [17592186198194 1020 #edb/ref 17592186299397 13194139534622 true] [17592186198194 1020 #edb/ref 17592186299404 13194139534622 true] [17592186198195 1020 #edb/ref 17592186299411 13194139534622 true] [17592186198195 1020 #edb/ref 17592186299418 13194139534622 true] [17592186198195 1020 #edb/ref 17592186299439 13194139534622 true] [17592186198697 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534622 true] [17592186198697 1100 "Which set is equivalent to $A = {x ∈ R: \\mid 2x + 5|= 13}$?" 13194139534622 false] [17592186198697 1100 "Which set is equivalent to $A={x\\in R:|2x+5|=13}?$" 13194139534622 true] [17592186198697 1145 "The elements of the given set are the real numbers that satisfy the equation $|2x+5|=13.$ So, we first need to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|2x+5| & =13 \\\\ 2x+5 & =\\pm 13 \\\\ 2x & =-5\\pm 13 \\\\ x & =\\frac{-5\\pm 13}{2} \\\\ x & =-9,4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solutions are $x=-9$ and $x=4,$ and both of these solutions are real numbers.\n\nTherefore, we can write the given set as\n\n$$\nA={-9,4}.\n$$" 13194139534622 true] [17592186198700 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534622 true] [17592186198700 1100 "Which set is equivalent to $A = {x ∈ Q: \\sin (2πx) = 0}$?" 13194139534622 false] [17592186198700 1100 "Which set is equivalent to $A={x\\in Q\\,:\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi x)=0}?$" 13194139534622 true] [17592186198700 1145 "Notice that the solutions to the equation\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi x)=0\n$$\n\n are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\pi x & =n\\pi  \\\\ 2x & =n \\\\ x & =\\frac{n}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $n\\in Z.$ \n\nSubstituting different values of $n,$ we see that the solutions are\n\n$$\nx=0,\\,\\pm \\frac{1}{2},\\,\\pm 1,\\,\\pm \\frac{3}{2},\\,…\n$$\n\nTherefore, our set $A$ is equivalent to \n\n$$\nA={0,\\,\\pm \\frac{1}{2},\\,\\pm 1,\\,\\pm \\frac{3}{2},\\,…}.\n$$" 13194139534622 true] [17592186198703 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534622 true] [17592186198703 1100 "Which set is equivalent to $A = {x ∈ R: \\cos (2x) = 1}$?" 13194139534622 false] [17592186198703 1100 "Which set is equivalent to $A={x\\in R:\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)=1}?$" 13194139534622 true] [17592186198703 1145 "Notice that the solutions to the equation\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)=1\n$$\n\n are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & =2n\\pi  \\\\ x & =n\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $n\\in Z.$ \n\nSubstituting different values of $n,$ we see that the solutions are\n\n$$\nx=0,\\,\\pm \\pi ,\\,\\pm 2\\pi ,\\,\\pm 3\\pi ,\\,…\n$$\n\nTherefore, our set $A$ is equivalent to \n\n$$\nA={0,\\pm \\pi ,\\pm 2\\pi ,\\pm 3\\pi ,…}.\n$$" 13194139534622 true] [17592186299341 1017 #edb/ref 17592186299342 13194139534622 true] [17592186299341 1089 "q-180759" 13194139534622 true] [17592186299341 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534622 true] [17592186299341 1100 "Which set is equivalent to $A={n\\in Z:5n+25=10}?$" 13194139534622 true] [17592186299341 1113 #uuid "35088702-98d7-583f-be4f-fdccb10ce1cb" 13194139534622 true] [17592186299341 1145 "The elements of the given set are the integers that satisfy the equation $5n+25=10.$ \n\nSo, we first need to solve our equation for $n:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5n+25 & =10 \\\\ 5n & =-15 \\\\ n & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution is $n=-3,$ which is an integer.\n\nTherefore, we can write the given set as\n\n$$\nA={-3}.\n$$" 13194139534622 true] [17592186299342 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299343 13194139534622 true] [17592186299342 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299344 13194139534622 true] [17592186299342 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299345 13194139534622 true] [17592186299342 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299346 13194139534622 true] [17592186299342 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299347 13194139534622 true] [17592186299342 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534622 true] [17592186299342 1041 "selection" 13194139534622 true] [17592186299342 1104 #edb/ref 17592186299347 13194139534622 true] [17592186299342 1110 #uuid "a1cc441c-f2b8-5191-aed3-bff2af15254a" 13194139534622 true] [17592186299343 1034 "{-5,2,10}" 13194139534622 true] [17592186299343 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 131941